  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A solid cylinder is released from rest from the top of an inclined plane of inclination <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. If the cylinder rolls without slipping, its speed upon reaching the bottom of the inclined plane is ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f1512277-f579-41e7-9318-318cf103cbfb-9896745.PNG\" style=\"width: 295px; height: 200px;\" />&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let speed of cylinder upon reaching the bottom of the inclined plane be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>.</p><p>Here, gain in kinetic energy<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>loss in potential energy</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>I</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mstyle><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>sin</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p>For pure rolling,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mstyle><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>sin</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>sin</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Putting the values, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
